1
00:00:06,405 --> 00:00:07,507
BOY: Hey you!

2
00:00:07,607 --> 00:00:10,009
DIVER: How many of you?

3
00:00:10,109 --> 00:00:12,011
 NARRATOR: For
 almost three weeks,

4
00:00:12,111 --> 00:00:15,514
 13 young lives hang
 in the balance.

5
00:00:16,482 --> 00:00:19,552
JASON: We didn't want
them to die and we didn't
want to die ourselves.

6
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:24,391
 NARRATOR: Then,
 against all the odds.

7
00:00:26,092 --> 00:00:29,162
 REPORTER (over TV):
 Mission impossible has
 become mission incredible!

8
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:36,002
 NARRATOR: One of the
 greatest rescues of all time.

9
00:00:37,369 --> 00:00:39,372
PASAKORN: It was
like a miracle

10
00:00:42,108 --> 00:00:44,109
NARRATOR: But questions remain.

11
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,579
 How did the boys get trapped?

12
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:49,716
 Why was it so hard
 to rescue them?

13
00:00:51,183 --> 00:00:53,052
MARTYN: The prospect
of a diving rescue was

14
00:00:53,152 --> 00:00:55,254
hideous from the outset.

15
00:00:55,354 --> 00:00:57,790
NARRATOR: And how was it done?

16
00:00:57,890 --> 00:01:00,192
CHRIS: Nothing like this
has ever happened before.

17
00:01:00,292 --> 00:01:02,629
JASON: Everything
was experimental.

18
00:01:03,896 --> 00:01:06,699
 NARRATOR: Now, with
 unprecedented access,

19
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:10,970
 a team of cavers conducts
 the first ever 3D scan of

20
00:01:11,070 --> 00:01:15,075
 Tham Luang, to
 uncover the answers.

21
00:01:17,977 --> 00:01:21,781
 Reconstructing the
 cave in perfect detail.

22
00:01:23,582 --> 00:01:25,318
ROO: We're going to be able
to actually show what that

23
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:27,553
passage was really like.

24
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:30,990
 NARRATOR: Transforming
 our understanding of the

25
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,493
 Thai Cave Rescue.

26
00:01:35,628 --> 00:01:37,563
VERN: If two of them came
out alive that would've

27
00:01:37,663 --> 00:01:39,599
been a good result.

28
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:47,173
(theme music plays).

29
00:01:52,178 --> 00:01:57,016
 NARRATOR: 13 young
 survivors and a moment
 few thought possible.

30
00:01:59,051 --> 00:02:00,352
BOY: Thank you so much.

31
00:02:00,452 --> 00:02:02,622
(speaking in native language).

32
00:02:02,722 --> 00:02:04,657
BOY: Thank you.

33
00:02:07,626 --> 00:02:10,963
NARRATOR: Leaving the hospital,
after an astonishing escape

34
00:02:11,063 --> 00:02:13,800
 and a terrifying ordeal.

35
00:02:26,445 --> 00:02:31,283
 25 days earlier, a school
 soccer team, the Wild Boars,

36
00:02:31,383 --> 00:02:35,054
 enjoyed a day trip
 to Tham Luang cave.

37
00:02:37,056 --> 00:02:41,227
 This is the last picture
 taken before they entered,

38
00:02:42,762 --> 00:02:45,932
 as night fell they
 were still inside.

39
00:02:54,039 --> 00:02:55,841
 REPORTER (over TV): A dozen
 member of a youth football

40
00:02:55,941 --> 00:02:58,510
 team and their
 coach are missing.

41
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:00,780
 REPORTER (over TV):
 Thought to be trapped
 in an underground cave.

42
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:03,082
NARONGSAK: Every
minute is important.

43
00:03:06,052 --> 00:03:08,555
NARRATOR: It would take 18 days,

44
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:13,959
 17 cave divers,

45
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:20,466
 200 air cylinders,
 a mile of rope,

46
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:24,204
 10,000 volunteers from
 over 20 countries,

47
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:27,773
 and one death,

48
00:03:28,307 --> 00:03:31,945
 before they could bring the
 Wild Boars out of the cave.

49
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:36,249
PASAKORN: The whole world
had their eyes upon us

50
00:03:36,349 --> 00:03:38,551
to see what we would do.

51
00:03:39,452 --> 00:03:41,020
 REPORTER (over TV): We begin
 tonight in Thailand with the

52
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:44,089
 life and death drama that's
 captivating the world.

53
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:46,859
 NARRATOR: The drama played
 out deep beneath the

54
00:03:46,959 --> 00:03:50,163
 Doi Nang Non Mountains
 of Northern Thailand.

55
00:04:02,307 --> 00:04:05,611
 Ten months later, a British
 team of cave explorers sets

56
00:04:05,711 --> 00:04:09,482
 out to conduct the first
 ever digital 3D survey

57
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:12,518
 inside Tham Luang cave.

58
00:04:18,157 --> 00:04:20,893
They will journey deep inside.

59
00:04:23,495 --> 00:04:26,164
 Hoping to discover
 the truth behind the

60
00:04:26,265 --> 00:04:29,469
 extraordinary events of 2018.

61
00:04:32,905 --> 00:04:36,976
 Leading the expedition is
 cave explorer Roo Walters.

62
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:41,380
ROO: When the divers
entered these caves,

63
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,848
they couldn't see a thing.

64
00:04:42,948 --> 00:04:44,650
They literally felt
their way through.

65
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:47,920
So we're going to show what
that passage was really like.

66
00:04:48,988 --> 00:04:50,956
 NARRATOR: Now that
 it's the dry season,

67
00:04:51,056 --> 00:04:55,295
 the team can penetrate
 the darkness to deploy
 the latest technology

68
00:04:57,797 --> 00:05:01,134
 and scan the cave in
 forensic detail.

69
00:05:03,736 --> 00:05:06,071
ROO: It'll start to reveal
just how clever and how

70
00:05:06,171 --> 00:05:09,108
inspirational this
whole exercise has been.

71
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:13,379
 NARRATOR: Even in
 the dry season,

72
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:16,349
 working here will
 be challenging.

73
00:05:22,421 --> 00:05:26,525
 After two hours, the survey
 team is in a squeeze.

74
00:05:27,226 --> 00:05:29,328
MAN: And then it
closes down again.

75
00:05:29,428 --> 00:05:30,997
 NARRATOR: Trying to reach
 the place where the boys

76
00:05:31,097 --> 00:05:34,267
 were eventually found,
 to begin their scan.

77
00:05:37,736 --> 00:05:39,438
MAN: How you doing there?

78
00:05:39,538 --> 00:05:41,140
Yeah?

79
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:44,310
 NARRATOR: They reach an
 area called Chamber 9.

80
00:05:44,410 --> 00:05:46,445
ROO: It changes
direction here Joe.

81
00:05:46,545 --> 00:05:48,681
JOE: Yeah.
Got a line up here.

82
00:05:50,882 --> 00:05:55,688
 NARRATOR: This rope, put in
 place by the rescue divers.

83
00:05:55,788 --> 00:05:59,826
 To help guide them
 through the silty water.

84
00:06:06,031 --> 00:06:07,466
JOE: Oh. Wow.

85
00:06:07,566 --> 00:06:11,371
ROO: Wow look at this!
It's the end of the line Joe.

86
00:06:16,175 --> 00:06:19,412
 NARRATOR: It was here
 the boys took refuge.

87
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,582
JOE: That's quite
something isn't it?

88
00:06:23,682 --> 00:06:27,787
ROO: That really
is something...

89
00:06:29,755 --> 00:06:31,190
Gosh!

90
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:34,460
 NARRATOR: Left behind, foil
 blankets and remnants of

91
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:38,197
 survival from 18
 days underground.

92
00:06:40,065 --> 00:06:43,068
JOE: Wow. Not a lot
of space is there.

93
00:06:43,168 --> 00:06:44,903
ROO: It's not a lot of space.

94
00:06:45,003 --> 00:06:48,707
NARRATOR: And an insignia, left
by the four Thai Navy Seals

95
00:06:48,807 --> 00:06:52,211
 who joined the boys on
 this muddy ledge for 8 days.

96
00:06:53,312 --> 00:06:55,715
ROO: This is incredible,
absolutely incredible.

97
00:06:55,815 --> 00:06:57,750
JOE: It's something
else isn't it?

98
00:06:57,850 --> 00:07:00,486
ROO: It's emotional, it is.

99
00:07:00,786 --> 00:07:04,256
 NARRATOR: They can now
 start scanning the cave.

100
00:07:04,790 --> 00:07:08,494
 Sending out 300,000
 laser beams a second

101
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:12,632
and recording every reflection
back from the cave walls.

102
00:07:14,099 --> 00:07:16,535
 The team hopes its data
 will explain exactly how

103
00:07:16,635 --> 00:07:19,138
 the boys got trapped.

104
00:07:29,715 --> 00:07:33,352
 Ten months earlier, the first
 rescue team was on site.

105
00:07:34,186 --> 00:07:37,990
 A mile inside the cave they
 made an alarming discovery.

106
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:42,260
The passage they knew the boys
had taken just hours earlier

107
00:07:42,361 --> 00:07:45,398
 was now, full of muddy water.

108
00:07:46,065 --> 00:07:48,200
 Where had it come from?

109
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:51,537
 And why had it
 risen so quickly?

110
00:07:59,211 --> 00:08:02,881
To find out, the survey team
must scan the cave system from

111
00:08:02,981 --> 00:08:07,119
 where the boys were trapped,
 all the way to the entrance.

112
00:08:09,522 --> 00:08:11,857
 The team works its way
 through the tunnels,

113
00:08:11,957 --> 00:08:14,526
 scanning every
 crack and fissure.

114
00:08:14,626 --> 00:08:17,029
ROO: Alright Joe?
JOE: Yeah all good.

115
00:08:17,696 --> 00:08:19,998
 NARRATOR: After half a mile
 they reach a point they think

116
00:08:20,098 --> 00:08:23,669
 is critical, called
 Sam Yek Junction.

117
00:08:26,205 --> 00:08:28,140
ROO: I think this must
be Sam Yek Junction guys.

118
00:08:28,241 --> 00:08:30,209
JOE: Yeah.

119
00:08:30,776 --> 00:08:34,580
 NARRATOR: The data
 they collect at Sam Yek
 junction will be vital.

120
00:08:42,454 --> 00:08:45,257
 Feeding it into powerful
 computer software,

121
00:08:45,357 --> 00:08:49,461
 we can now recreate the first
 section of the cave system,

122
00:08:49,561 --> 00:08:53,466
 in perfect 3
 dimensional detail.

123
00:08:54,866 --> 00:09:00,006
 This is Chamber 9 where the
 boys were finally trapped...

124
00:09:02,374 --> 00:09:06,345
 And this, the half mile
 long passage back...

125
00:09:10,516 --> 00:09:13,986
 to Sam Yek junction.

126
00:09:24,296 --> 00:09:28,333
 But a closer look at
 Sam Yek reveals a clue.

127
00:09:29,234 --> 00:09:33,706
 Another tunnel,
 Monks series, joins the
 main cave system here.

128
00:09:37,309 --> 00:09:41,013
 In the rainy season when
 these caves fill with water,

129
00:09:41,113 --> 00:09:46,452
 Sam Yek becomes the
 meeting point for two
 underground rivers.

130
00:09:52,324 --> 00:09:55,060
Water finds its way through
the cracks and channels of the

131
00:09:55,160 --> 00:09:59,065
 limestone mountains into
 Tham Luang's cave system.

132
00:10:01,967 --> 00:10:05,004
VERN: This mountain is just
a big sponge and during the

133
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:09,208
rainy season there's a huge
volume of water travels

134
00:10:09,308 --> 00:10:12,678
through Tham Luang Cave,
basically like a big river.

135
00:10:16,549 --> 00:10:19,050
 NARRATOR: Back in 2018 when
 the boys and their coach

136
00:10:19,151 --> 00:10:22,722
 started exploring, there
 was no sign of rain.

137
00:10:25,391 --> 00:10:29,795
They had no difficulty walking
through Sam Yek Junction.

138
00:10:34,066 --> 00:10:38,037
 But outside, the weather
 was changing fast.

139
00:10:40,238 --> 00:10:44,176
 The heavy monsoon rains
 had arrived weeks early.

140
00:10:45,678 --> 00:10:49,949
 Almost an inch of
 rain fell in an hour.

141
00:10:57,590 --> 00:11:00,793
 Water seeped through
 the limestone mountains,

142
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:04,163
 funneling down
 into Tham Luang.

143
00:11:07,232 --> 00:11:10,936
 And then at Sam Yek
 junction, the other passage,

144
00:11:11,036 --> 00:11:15,474
 Monks Series, brought yet
 more water into the cave.

145
00:11:23,582 --> 00:11:27,953
 At Sam Yek's narrowest
 point the junction
 filled in just an hour,

146
00:11:28,053 --> 00:11:31,490
 flooding it to the roof.

147
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:40,199
 The boys were now sealed
 inside the cave system
 with no way out.

148
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:47,205
ROO: Sam Yek is the crux of
this story and the 3D model

149
00:11:47,305 --> 00:11:51,042
clearly shows how that water
then flooded the cave and

150
00:11:51,142 --> 00:11:53,345
entrapped the boys.

151
00:11:54,213 --> 00:11:56,081
VERN: It was very isolated.

152
00:11:56,181 --> 00:11:58,984
There was actually
nowhere for them to go.

153
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:03,822
 NARRATOR: As rain
 continued to fall...

154
00:12:03,922 --> 00:12:06,292
 water levels rose further.

155
00:12:07,459 --> 00:12:12,298
 Forcing the boys deeper
 inside as they looked
 for higher ground.

156
00:12:13,699 --> 00:12:16,802
 So how did they survive?

157
00:12:22,641 --> 00:12:29,047
♪ ♪

158
00:12:30,015 --> 00:12:31,950
 NARRATOR: Desperate local
 officials called in the

159
00:12:32,050 --> 00:12:35,721
 country's elite divers
 to search for the boys.

160
00:12:37,122 --> 00:12:39,492
 The Thai Navy Seals...

161
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:46,165
 But the still rising
 water and strong currents
 forced them back.

162
00:12:48,099 --> 00:12:49,601
 OMAR (over TV): Relentless
 rain is jeopardizing an

163
00:12:49,701 --> 00:12:51,370
 already risky operation.

164
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:52,838
 REPORTER (over TV): They
 believe that there has been

165
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:55,006
 flash flooding inside.

166
00:12:55,106 --> 00:12:58,778
 OMAR (over TV): The
 desperate race now is
 to find another way in.

167
00:13:04,149 --> 00:13:07,419
 NARRATOR: Above ground
 armies of cavers scoured the

168
00:13:07,519 --> 00:13:10,956
 mountains looking for a way
 into the cave from above.

169
00:13:13,692 --> 00:13:15,828
 The search was
 gathering momentum.

170
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:25,370
 On day 9, a breakthrough.

171
00:13:26,004 --> 00:13:29,241
 Electric pumps reduced
 the water levels.

172
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:35,414
 Making it safe enough for
 the Navy Seals to dive.

173
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:42,488
 They hunted for signs of
 life, deep inside and laid a

174
00:13:42,588 --> 00:13:46,292
 guideline to mark their
 route back to safety.

175
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:50,896
JOSH: We didn't really know
exactly where the boys were.

176
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,698
I thought it was probably more
likely they were dead than

177
00:13:53,798 --> 00:13:56,202
alive at that point.

178
00:13:57,602 --> 00:14:00,539
 NARRATOR: But
 they weren't dead.

179
00:14:00,639 --> 00:14:03,342
 So how did they survive?

180
00:14:07,379 --> 00:14:11,417
 Revisiting the data
 of the flooded cave
 reveals the answer.

181
00:14:13,252 --> 00:14:15,454
 This is Sam Yek.

182
00:14:15,554 --> 00:14:19,758
 Where the water rose quickly,
 trapping more water behind it.

183
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:30,035
 But here in Chamber 9, the
 boys managed to find refuge.

184
00:14:32,137 --> 00:14:36,442
 Discovering a solitary
 shaft off the main passage.

185
00:14:37,176 --> 00:14:41,580
 They scrambled up 14 feet
 above the water line.

186
00:14:45,319 --> 00:14:49,554
 It's a safe haven, in
 a dark lofty hollow,

187
00:14:49,654 --> 00:14:54,193
 that reaches 124 feet
 above the rest of the cave.

188
00:14:56,795 --> 00:14:59,798
 This was the only space in
 the cave in which the boys

189
00:14:59,898 --> 00:15:03,002
 could have survived.

190
00:15:06,338 --> 00:15:10,409
 But a closer look at
 the cave data shows an
 intriguing anomaly,

191
00:15:12,210 --> 00:15:16,181
 at the highest point of the
 boy's refuge a small cavity,

192
00:15:16,281 --> 00:15:20,452
 two and a half feet
 wide and 9 feet long.

193
00:15:23,522 --> 00:15:25,791
ROO: It doesn't look like a
normal piece of cave it really

194
00:15:25,891 --> 00:15:28,927
sticks out and that's
because it isn't.

195
00:15:29,027 --> 00:15:31,897
 NARRATOR: Revealed in the
 data, for the first time,

196
00:15:31,997 --> 00:15:34,733
 a tunnel the boys dug out.

197
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,902
ROO: It's amazing.

198
00:15:37,002 --> 00:15:38,404
Little stone tools
are still there,

199
00:15:38,504 --> 00:15:42,408
scratches in the sides of
the walls are still there.

200
00:15:45,677 --> 00:15:47,646
What must have been going
through their minds as they dug

201
00:15:47,746 --> 00:15:51,050
with no idea of how far
underground they are.

202
00:15:53,652 --> 00:15:57,389
 NARRATOR: Could the boys
 have dug themselves out
 from Chamber 9?

203
00:15:57,489 --> 00:16:00,658
How far underground were they?

204
00:16:01,859 --> 00:16:05,230
 To find out, the team need
 to do more than just survey

205
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:08,067
 inside the cave.

206
00:16:12,704 --> 00:16:16,875
They must also discover
exactly where Tham Luang lies,

207
00:16:16,975 --> 00:16:19,845
 beneath the mountains.

208
00:16:21,947 --> 00:16:25,484
 The investigation
 takes to the air.

209
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:32,191
ROO: We can connect the cave
3D model to the surface model

210
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:34,993
and from that we'll actually
be able to work out exactly

211
00:16:35,093 --> 00:16:37,830
how far the boys
were underground.

212
00:16:40,832 --> 00:16:44,169
NARRATOR: Combining this aerial
data with the underground scan,

213
00:16:44,269 --> 00:16:47,506
 we can pinpoint exactly
 where the boys were

214
00:16:47,606 --> 00:16:51,143
 in the mountain,

215
00:16:51,243 --> 00:16:54,880
 one and half miles from
 the cave entrance,

216
00:16:56,548 --> 00:17:01,219
 and above them, lay 2,000
 feet of solid rock.

217
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:04,656
 Accurately revealed
 for the first time,

218
00:17:04,757 --> 00:17:08,660
 the boys' complete isolation.

219
00:17:10,495 --> 00:17:14,033
 Digging a tunnel was futile.

220
00:17:15,633 --> 00:17:18,937
ROO: What we've discovered, is
just how remote the boys were.

221
00:17:19,037 --> 00:17:22,074
It must have been
terrifying for them.

222
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:35,954
 NARRATOR: Dive teams
 had searched the
 flooded cave for days.

223
00:17:38,757 --> 00:17:41,393
 Two British cave-divers
 joined them,

224
00:17:41,493 --> 00:17:44,797
helping to lay more guideline.

225
00:17:46,865 --> 00:17:50,269
 Then, a mile and
 a half inside...

226
00:18:14,926 --> 00:18:16,828
 REPORTER (over TV):
 Dramatic scenes in Thailand.

227
00:18:16,928 --> 00:18:19,164
 REPORTER (over TV): Against
 all odds rescuers in Thailand

228
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:21,699
 have found 12 missing boys.

229
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:24,603
 REPORTER (over TV): Well
 what an amazing day.

230
00:18:27,505 --> 00:18:29,541
REPORTER (over TV): For family
members pure elation after a

231
00:18:29,641 --> 00:18:32,444
 heart-breaking waiting game.

232
00:18:35,847 --> 00:18:38,549
 NARRATOR: The boys had
 survived underground for

233
00:18:38,649 --> 00:18:42,120
 10 days with only the water
 dripping from the cave walls

234
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:45,056
 to sustain them.

235
00:18:46,057 --> 00:18:49,327
 Within hours the Thai
 Navy Seals delivered food,

236
00:18:49,427 --> 00:18:53,365
 medicine and foil blankets
 to prevent hypothermia.

237
00:18:54,399 --> 00:18:58,369
 But one thing was on
 everyone's minds...

238
00:18:59,237 --> 00:19:04,643
VERN: Very quickly we
realized that our problem
was only just beginning.

239
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:08,547
JOSH: Finding them
is one thing but what
are you gonna do next?

240
00:19:09,147 --> 00:19:12,518
 NARRATOR: The Thai
 Authorities were desperate
 to find a simple solution.

241
00:19:15,186 --> 00:19:18,290
 But it would take another 8
 days of nerve-wracking and

242
00:19:18,390 --> 00:19:21,893
 dangerous work to
 get the boys out.

243
00:19:22,193 --> 00:19:25,697
MARTYN: Little did we know
how long and how complex that

244
00:19:25,797 --> 00:19:28,267
operation was going to become.

245
00:19:33,405 --> 00:19:36,841
 NARRATOR: The Thai Authorities
 identified three options...

246
00:19:37,475 --> 00:19:41,179
 One: wait for the monsoon
 rains to pass so the boys

247
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:44,015
 could walk out of a dry cave.

248
00:19:44,115 --> 00:19:47,085
 But that would take months.

249
00:19:48,787 --> 00:19:52,657
 Two: find another route
 into the cave from above.

250
00:19:52,757 --> 00:19:58,030
 But a week of mountain
 searches discovered
 only dead ends.

251
00:20:00,465 --> 00:20:05,871
 That left option three, the
 most extreme-sounding of all.

252
00:20:07,905 --> 00:20:09,374
 REPORTER (over TV): Are
 they gonna have to learn
 how to scuba dive

253
00:20:09,474 --> 00:20:12,844
their way out of there I
mean that's really a tall order.

254
00:20:13,545 --> 00:20:16,114
 REPORTER (over TV): Yeah
 it's crazy isn't it.

255
00:20:17,048 --> 00:20:19,685
PASAKORN: We came to the
conclusion that the only way

256
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:23,188
to bring the children out was
the same way they went in.

257
00:20:25,823 --> 00:20:29,494
MARTYN: The prospect
of a diving rescue was
hideous from the outset.

258
00:20:30,295 --> 00:20:33,064
 NARRATOR: What is it about
 diving in Tham Luang that

259
00:20:33,164 --> 00:20:36,468
 makes it just so dangerous?

260
00:20:44,442 --> 00:20:46,945
NARRATOR: It takes three weeks
for the survey team to scan

261
00:20:47,045 --> 00:20:49,714
 Tham Luang cave.

262
00:20:50,248 --> 00:20:54,853
 All the way from Chamber
 9 to the cave entrance.

263
00:20:58,923 --> 00:21:02,293
 The boys were one and
 a half miles inside.

264
00:21:02,393 --> 00:21:06,364
But they were safe, and divers
had managed to navigate the

265
00:21:06,464 --> 00:21:09,067
flooded tunnels to reach them.

266
00:21:10,268 --> 00:21:14,273
 So why was it so
 difficult to get them out?

267
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:18,910
To understand, takes big data.

268
00:21:19,678 --> 00:21:22,813
 The team pieces together
 nearly 400 scans and

269
00:21:22,914 --> 00:21:25,684
builds a virtual cave system...

270
00:21:27,585 --> 00:21:29,320
ROO: So this is full res.

271
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:32,123
JOE: The detail in
that roof is fantastic.

272
00:21:32,524 --> 00:21:36,361
 NARRATOR: A new visualization
 of this underground world.

273
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:40,598
ROO: We will start to be able
to show everybody what this

274
00:21:40,698 --> 00:21:42,634
cave is really like.

275
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:44,836
It is gonna be quite magical.

276
00:21:44,936 --> 00:21:48,774
NARRATOR: With the world's first
3D digital survey of Tham Luang

277
00:21:48,874 --> 00:21:53,178
 we can reveal the second
 section of the cave system,

278
00:21:53,278 --> 00:21:56,581
 all the way from
 Chamber 9 to the entrance.

279
00:21:59,851 --> 00:22:04,423
 8.7 billion data points,

280
00:22:05,656 --> 00:22:08,927
 more than 7000 photographs,

281
00:22:10,128 --> 00:22:16,468
 come together to build
 the flooded cave as it
 was in July 2018.

282
00:22:23,208 --> 00:22:28,647
 Draining its water,
 for the first time....

283
00:22:33,719 --> 00:22:38,290
 Exposes all of its
 subterranean secrets.

284
00:22:45,463 --> 00:22:49,467
 This is Chamber 9 to Sam Yek

285
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:53,171
 and now, the rest
 of Tham Luang cave,

286
00:23:00,245 --> 00:23:04,549
 a narrow tunnel, that
 widens to the entrance.

287
00:23:07,118 --> 00:23:10,956
 All together one
 and a half miles,

288
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:14,359
 the boys' only route out.

289
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:25,703
 Adding the water level of
 the time to the digital map

290
00:23:25,803 --> 00:23:29,908
 reveals why Tham Luang's
 passages can be so lethal.

291
00:23:32,177 --> 00:23:36,014
 In some places,
 underground canals formed.

292
00:23:37,282 --> 00:23:40,451
 In others, the cave
 flooded to its roof,

293
00:23:40,552 --> 00:23:44,289
 fully submerging the passage,

294
00:23:46,224 --> 00:23:50,095
in five sections known as sumps.

295
00:23:53,431 --> 00:23:59,037
 The longest sump lay
 next to Chamber 9,
 over 1,000 feet long,

296
00:24:01,472 --> 00:24:05,143
 the length of seven
 Olympic swimming pools,

297
00:24:07,144 --> 00:24:10,615
 taken together there were
 half a mile of sumps,

298
00:24:10,715 --> 00:24:15,620
 standing between
 the boys and safety.

299
00:24:20,358 --> 00:24:24,830
 And the visibility
 was almost zero.

300
00:24:26,197 --> 00:24:29,600
 The only way to escape
 Chamber 9 was a long

301
00:24:29,700 --> 00:24:32,737
 perilous cave dive
 with air tanks,

302
00:24:34,305 --> 00:24:36,841
 a potentially deadly option,

303
00:24:36,941 --> 00:24:41,179
 even for Thailand's diving
 elite, the Navy Seals.

304
00:24:43,014 --> 00:24:46,050
JONGKLAI: The Thai Navy Seals
who assisted with the rescue

305
00:24:46,150 --> 00:24:48,853
had only trained in open seas.

306
00:24:48,953 --> 00:24:52,357
They'd never dived in
very narrow spaces.

307
00:24:56,961 --> 00:24:59,931
 NARRATOR: They needed
 specialist help.

308
00:25:00,532 --> 00:25:03,467
 A local caver, Vern Unsworth,
 had been part of the

309
00:25:03,568 --> 00:25:06,604
 search and rescue
 mission since day one.

310
00:25:07,772 --> 00:25:12,143
 After seven years exploring
 Tham Luang he well understood

311
00:25:12,243 --> 00:25:14,579
 the challenge ahead.

312
00:25:14,679 --> 00:25:18,683
VERN: We needed expert people
out here, and, you know,

313
00:25:18,783 --> 00:25:21,318
at the end of the day it
was the right decision.

314
00:25:21,418 --> 00:25:23,888
 NARRATOR: He gave the Thai
 authorities a list of some of

315
00:25:23,988 --> 00:25:27,125
 Britain's most
 experienced cave divers.

316
00:25:35,166 --> 00:25:40,705
 An elite team arrived,
 including John Velanthon,

317
00:25:41,906 --> 00:25:47,345
 Rick Stanton, Jason
 Mallinson and Chris Jewell.

318
00:25:50,147 --> 00:25:54,419
 They are among just a small
 group of people in the world

319
00:25:54,519 --> 00:25:58,723
 who had the unique skills
 needed inside Tham Luang.

320
00:26:00,491 --> 00:26:02,693
CHRIS: When we realized this
was the best chance of the

321
00:26:02,793 --> 00:26:04,596
boys getting out alive,

322
00:26:04,696 --> 00:26:07,365
then we were determined
to give it our best shot.

323
00:26:10,835 --> 00:26:14,405
 NARRATOR: A rescue
 plan developed.

324
00:26:15,172 --> 00:26:19,110
 From the entrance, the first
 half mile of cave was dry.

325
00:26:19,210 --> 00:26:21,612
 At the end of it, Chamber 3.

326
00:26:21,712 --> 00:26:24,449
 This would be dive base.

327
00:26:26,518 --> 00:26:28,986
 From here, four cave
 divers would head deeper

328
00:26:29,086 --> 00:26:31,489
 into the flooded cave.

329
00:26:31,589 --> 00:26:35,193
 Three hours later they
 would reach the soccer team.

330
00:26:36,027 --> 00:26:38,930
 Four boys would be
 equipped with scuba gear.

331
00:26:40,264 --> 00:26:44,368
 Then each diver would
 return with one boy

332
00:26:44,468 --> 00:26:47,605
 at 30-minute intervals.

333
00:26:48,006 --> 00:26:51,308
 If everything went to plan,
 it would take a full day to

334
00:26:51,408 --> 00:26:54,145
 extract four boys.

335
00:26:55,413 --> 00:26:57,715
 On their way out, each
 diver and boy would need

336
00:26:57,815 --> 00:27:00,317
 replacement air tanks.

337
00:27:01,452 --> 00:27:07,158
 So, they placed 50 of them
 throughout the cave and seven

338
00:27:07,258 --> 00:27:10,728
 support divers would wait
 between sumps to haul

339
00:27:10,828 --> 00:27:14,666
 equipment and provide
 medical backup.

340
00:27:16,668 --> 00:27:20,437
 It was a rescue
 plan like no other.

341
00:27:20,971 --> 00:27:23,174
CHRIS: The situation in
Thailand was unprecedented.

342
00:27:23,274 --> 00:27:25,643
Nothing like this has, has
ever happened before.

343
00:27:25,743 --> 00:27:28,513
Not those kind of distances and
certainly that number of people.

344
00:27:38,422 --> 00:27:41,459
 NARRATOR: There were nearly
 100 divers on site.

345
00:27:44,161 --> 00:27:49,100
 Emergency services, the
 US Army and volunteers,

346
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:52,203
 also out in force.

347
00:27:52,303 --> 00:27:57,242
 All prepared and
 rehearsed for the first
 underwater extraction.

348
00:28:04,616 --> 00:28:08,519
 At 1:30 AM, tragedy.

349
00:28:09,287 --> 00:28:10,988
 VAUSE (over TV): Breaking
 news out of Thailand.

350
00:28:11,089 --> 00:28:14,693
 Where a former Thai Navy
 Seal has died during
 rescue operations.

351
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:19,563
 NARRATOR: Saman Kunan, seen
 here with the rescue team,

352
00:28:19,663 --> 00:28:22,867
 was on an overnight mission
 to place air cylinders

353
00:28:22,967 --> 00:28:25,169
 inside the cave.

354
00:28:25,269 --> 00:28:28,406
 It's believed his
 own air ran out.

355
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:31,810
 REPORTER (over TV): This has
 taken on a whole new level of

356
00:28:31,910 --> 00:28:35,647
 seriousness, there's a sense
 of mourning here today.

357
00:28:37,482 --> 00:28:38,983
 REPORTER (over TV): It's
 raised serious doubts about

358
00:28:39,083 --> 00:28:42,587
 how they'll get the 12 boys
 and their coach out alive.

359
00:28:44,054 --> 00:28:48,192
 NARRATOR: How would the boys
 escape a cave that can kill

360
00:28:48,292 --> 00:28:50,862
 even the best divers?

361
00:28:57,735 --> 00:29:01,039
 NARRATOR: Diving in Tham Luang
 had already taken one life.

362
00:29:03,073 --> 00:29:05,676
 It was an even greater
 threat to children who

363
00:29:05,776 --> 00:29:08,513
 had never dived before.

364
00:29:09,647 --> 00:29:13,651
 But the greatest danger of
 all, lay not in the cave,

365
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:17,454
 but in the heads of
 the boys themselves.

366
00:29:18,555 --> 00:29:21,793
MARTYN: If you take
an inexperienced
person underwater

367
00:29:23,227 --> 00:29:27,999
then there is a high probability
that they're going to panic.

368
00:29:30,468 --> 00:29:34,072
How were they going to cope
with something as traumatic

369
00:29:34,172 --> 00:29:37,108
as the prospect of diving,
where you can't see

370
00:29:37,208 --> 00:29:40,011
your hand in front of your face?

371
00:29:41,678 --> 00:29:43,614
JASON: If they'd have panicked
underwater they could have not

372
00:29:43,714 --> 00:29:46,017
only killed themselves,
they could have dragged our

373
00:29:46,117 --> 00:29:49,453
regulators out of our mouths
we didn't want them to die and

374
00:29:49,554 --> 00:29:52,056
we didn't want
to die ourselves.

375
00:29:58,763 --> 00:30:02,533
 NARRATOR: So the divers
 made the most radical
 decision of the rescue.

376
00:30:02,633 --> 00:30:05,670
 To sedate the children.

377
00:30:06,838 --> 00:30:09,740
JASON: It was a consensus
amongst all the divers.

378
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:13,444
We weren't going to risk doing
it without them being sedated.

379
00:30:14,679 --> 00:30:17,248
 NARRATOR: Doctors tailored a
 different mix of anesthetics

380
00:30:17,348 --> 00:30:21,052
 for every child, depending
 on age and weight.

381
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:27,525
 No one had ever attempted
 to dive with unconscious
 children before.

382
00:30:28,626 --> 00:30:31,929
MARTYN: Having to sedate these
youngsters to such a level

383
00:30:32,029 --> 00:30:35,633
that they were incapacitated
but remain alive,

384
00:30:35,733 --> 00:30:38,836
and then be thrust into
the cold water was an

385
00:30:38,936 --> 00:30:41,072
extremely risky proposition.

386
00:30:41,172 --> 00:30:42,873
JASON: As we were planning
it we were thinking,

387
00:30:42,973 --> 00:30:45,976
you know it could be some of
these kids that are gonna die.

388
00:30:46,911 --> 00:30:49,580
 NARRATOR: And as our
 cave data reveal,

389
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:52,516
 using a sedative left
 the cave divers with a

390
00:30:52,616 --> 00:30:55,153
 further complication.

391
00:30:58,689 --> 00:31:01,325
 To extract each boy
 through the five sumps

392
00:31:01,426 --> 00:31:04,796
would take three to five hours.

393
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:11,436
 But a safe dose of the
 sedative would last
 just an hour or less.

394
00:31:18,343 --> 00:31:21,445
 And so, to prevent
 the boys from waking,

395
00:31:21,545 --> 00:31:24,449
 the divers would
 have no option,

396
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:28,319
 they'd have to inject
 them during the rescue.

397
00:31:29,587 --> 00:31:32,223
JASON: Never actually
done it before and yes
it was the first time.

398
00:31:32,323 --> 00:31:34,391
I was quite nervous obviously.

399
00:31:34,491 --> 00:31:39,063
 NARRATOR: And they could
 do that only in the dry
 parts of the cave,

400
00:31:39,163 --> 00:31:43,201
 between sumps,
 not underwater...

401
00:31:45,402 --> 00:31:50,041
 Something that would bring
 diver Jason Mallinson
 close to disaster.

402
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:00,718
 Nature was not on
 the rescuer's side.

403
00:32:00,818 --> 00:32:03,220
 More rain was forecast.

404
00:32:03,621 --> 00:32:06,290
PASAKORN: If we didn't rescue
them immediately we might have

405
00:32:06,390 --> 00:32:08,492
had even bigger problems.

406
00:32:09,026 --> 00:32:11,262
 NARRATOR: They scheduled
 the extraction.

407
00:32:21,372 --> 00:32:24,408
 NARRATOR: As more
 monsoon rain closed in,

408
00:32:24,508 --> 00:32:27,678
 the divers headed
 inside Tham Luang.

409
00:32:28,246 --> 00:32:31,282
 The boys had been
 underground for 16 days.

410
00:32:33,150 --> 00:32:38,489
 The most dangerous cave
 diving rescue in history
 was about to begin...

411
00:32:40,124 --> 00:32:42,726
VERN: We honestly
believed that there would
be an attrition rate,

412
00:32:42,827 --> 00:32:45,028
if two of them came out
alive that would've

413
00:32:45,128 --> 00:32:47,164
been a good result.

414
00:32:47,264 --> 00:32:50,301
 NARRATOR: And the
 world was watching.

415
00:32:55,639 --> 00:32:58,743
 The rescuers began
 their dive to Chamber 9.

416
00:33:00,444 --> 00:33:03,748
 Jason Mallinson volunteered
 to run the first rescue.

417
00:33:06,283 --> 00:33:11,055
 The life in his hands was
 14 year old Prachak Sutham,

418
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:13,958
 nicknamed Note.

419
00:33:14,425 --> 00:33:17,194
JASON: Until that first
flooded section was traversed

420
00:33:17,294 --> 00:33:20,030
by myself and the boy, nothing
else could move forward

421
00:33:21,431 --> 00:33:24,835
 NARRATOR: Together they
 would discover if a
 rescue was possible.

422
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:29,339
 They fitted a single air tank
 to Note's chest and gave him a

423
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:32,610
 buoyancy vest with
 straps for Jason to hold.

424
00:33:35,079 --> 00:33:39,917
 In case contact was lost,
 a safety tether joined
 boy to rescuer.

425
00:33:42,086 --> 00:33:44,788
 To stop Note's mask
 being dislodged,

426
00:33:44,888 --> 00:33:48,325
 Jason would shield the boy's
 head with his own body and

427
00:33:48,425 --> 00:33:53,497
 finally, for both their sakes,
 Note's hands were tied to his

428
00:33:53,597 --> 00:33:56,601
 sides in case he awoke.

429
00:34:03,941 --> 00:34:08,746
 Around 1 PM Jason and Note
 began the first journey out.

430
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:13,918
 With the cave data
 we can do something
 impossible up to now.

431
00:34:17,421 --> 00:34:21,959
 Use technology to see through
 the muddy water to relive the

432
00:34:22,059 --> 00:34:26,397
 most dangerous cave
 diving rescue of all time.

433
00:34:27,598 --> 00:34:31,135
 And reveal Tham Luang in
 a way that even the divers

434
00:34:31,235 --> 00:34:34,304
 were unable to see.

435
00:34:35,172 --> 00:34:40,178
 This, the first sump, 1,000
 feet long, underwater.

436
00:34:41,878 --> 00:34:47,284
 And the dive line their
 only chance of finding
 their way to safety.

437
00:34:48,018 --> 00:34:49,553
JASON: The worst fear was
losing contact with the

438
00:34:49,653 --> 00:34:52,489
guideline and losing
contact with the boy.

439
00:34:52,589 --> 00:34:55,659
We felt a tremendous amount of
responsibility for the boys,

440
00:34:55,759 --> 00:34:59,363
a child's life that's in your
hands, a child who's asleep,

441
00:34:59,463 --> 00:35:02,333
a child underwater.

442
00:35:03,367 --> 00:35:05,870
I was nervous a
lot of the time.

443
00:35:07,138 --> 00:35:08,906
 NARRATOR: At half
 hour intervals,

444
00:35:09,006 --> 00:35:12,910
 three more divers
 entered the first sump
 with three more boys.

445
00:35:14,645 --> 00:35:16,981
 Not far behind
 Jason and Note,

446
00:35:17,081 --> 00:35:21,452
 were diver Chris Jewell
 and 15 year old Nick.

447
00:35:25,222 --> 00:35:29,459
 Separately each pair
 approached Tham Luang's
 first constriction.

448
00:35:30,060 --> 00:35:33,097
JASON: First time you
know about it is when
you hit the roof.

449
00:35:34,232 --> 00:35:37,434
 NARRATOR: A low passage,
 just 30 inches high,

450
00:35:37,534 --> 00:35:40,170
 little room for error.

451
00:35:40,704 --> 00:35:43,306
CHRIS: My back would be
against the cave roof and my

452
00:35:43,407 --> 00:35:46,243
chest would be against
the floor of the cave.

453
00:35:47,110 --> 00:35:49,680
 NARRATOR: The dive line was
 difficult to follow as it

454
00:35:49,780 --> 00:35:52,783
 meandered between
 the cave walls.

455
00:35:53,951 --> 00:35:56,186
CHRIS: I was often bouncing
off the rock and having to

456
00:35:56,286 --> 00:36:00,391
kind of back up and try
and go forward again
into different spaces.

457
00:36:01,559 --> 00:36:04,795
 NARRATOR: One after the other
 the divers felt their way

458
00:36:04,895 --> 00:36:08,399
 through the sumps carrying
 their precious cargo.

459
00:36:10,768 --> 00:36:14,171
CHRIS: We might knock the mask
off so we were trying to go

460
00:36:14,271 --> 00:36:18,242
through these small spaces
quite carefully, taking our time

461
00:36:19,577 --> 00:36:22,913
whilst holding onto the
dive line in one hand

462
00:36:23,013 --> 00:36:26,117
and holding onto the
child in the other hand.

463
00:36:29,252 --> 00:36:32,356
 NARRATOR: But the sedatives
 were beginning to wear off.

464
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:37,227
 Making an already difficult
 situation, life-threatening.

465
00:36:38,562 --> 00:36:42,199
JASON: You'd be diving along
underwater and you could feel
the hands twitching.

466
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:47,872
 NARRATOR: Revealed
 accurately; the scene of
 one perilous incident.

467
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:52,710
 Between dives, Jason
 was able to surface,

468
00:36:52,810 --> 00:36:56,113
 but he was still
 chest deep in water.

469
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:59,383
JASON: I was in a deep canal;
I was on my own and there was

470
00:36:59,483 --> 00:37:01,786
no dry place to put the boy
and I needed to inject the

471
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:04,655
sedative into his thigh.

472
00:37:05,322 --> 00:37:10,260
 NARRATOR: Ahead of them,
 the second sump, another
 1,000 feet underwater,

473
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:14,331
 Jason had no option but
 to inject the sedative

474
00:37:14,431 --> 00:37:17,067
 right where he was.

475
00:37:17,467 --> 00:37:20,204
JASON: I was trying to undo
the dry bag with two hands but

476
00:37:20,304 --> 00:37:22,572
keep control of
the child as well.

477
00:37:22,672 --> 00:37:24,641
It was quite hard to hold
him I had to sort of pin him

478
00:37:24,741 --> 00:37:27,611
against the wall with my leg,
try and get all the syringes

479
00:37:27,711 --> 00:37:30,281
out of the bag, they all
started floating around in the

480
00:37:30,381 --> 00:37:33,217
water and I'm trying to
get the, the syringes.

481
00:37:33,317 --> 00:37:34,885
I was quite nervous obviously,

482
00:37:34,985 --> 00:37:38,022
and I managed to
bring his leg up,

483
00:37:39,122 --> 00:37:41,259
put the sedative
into his leg.

484
00:37:49,633 --> 00:37:54,105
MARTYN: The whole thing
is really fraught with
mental strain.

485
00:37:55,038 --> 00:37:57,441
JASON: High stress,
that's for sure.

486
00:37:57,908 --> 00:38:00,243
 NARRATOR: After
 two grueling hours,

487
00:38:00,343 --> 00:38:03,113
 rescuers and boys had
 traveled through four sumps

488
00:38:03,213 --> 00:38:05,916
 along a mile of cave.

489
00:38:06,016 --> 00:38:08,385
 But it wasn't over.

490
00:38:08,485 --> 00:38:14,525
 Ahead lay a dive in the
 final sump and the tightest
 squeeze of them all.

491
00:38:20,430 --> 00:38:23,034
 NARRATOR: Following the dive
 line the survey team locates

492
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:25,903
 Tham Luang's
 worst pinch point.

493
00:38:26,203 --> 00:38:27,471
ROO: Look at this
constriction.

494
00:38:27,571 --> 00:38:28,906
MAN: Doesn't look very nice.

495
00:38:29,006 --> 00:38:30,975
ROO: Gosh that's small.

496
00:38:32,009 --> 00:38:36,147
 NARRATOR: How would a diver
 and a child fit through here?

497
00:38:41,618 --> 00:38:44,788
 The 3D data exposes
 the problem,

498
00:38:44,888 --> 00:38:48,259
 over 100 feet into
 the final sump.

499
00:38:50,694 --> 00:38:54,699
 The dive line goes through
 a curtain of stalactites.

500
00:38:56,133 --> 00:39:00,504
 A gap just 20 inches wide
 at its narrowest point.

501
00:39:02,206 --> 00:39:04,307
JASON: You couldn't fit
through the stalactites.

502
00:39:04,408 --> 00:39:07,712
It's certainly the
most difficult part of
the cave to navigate.

503
00:39:09,346 --> 00:39:13,417
 NARRATOR: But the data
 reveals something the
 divers couldn't see.

504
00:39:14,318 --> 00:39:18,889
 Below the dive line, a
 wider passage, 6 feet deep.

505
00:39:20,190 --> 00:39:24,528
 But making use of this space,
 by feeling a way through,

506
00:39:24,628 --> 00:39:26,697
 was risky.

507
00:39:27,298 --> 00:39:29,499
CHRIS: You have to back out,
pull the line and find the

508
00:39:29,599 --> 00:39:31,702
biggest space that you
could work your way round.

509
00:39:31,802 --> 00:39:33,670
JASON: We had to
pull the line down,

510
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:35,973
stretch it down and go
under the stalactites.

511
00:39:36,073 --> 00:39:39,009
NARRATOR: By pulling down on
the dive line the divers could

512
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:41,578
 swim beneath the pinch point.

513
00:39:41,678 --> 00:39:46,450
 But the extra tension
 on the line made it
 harder to hold on to.

514
00:39:48,118 --> 00:39:50,187
JASON: There was always
potential for it to slip

515
00:39:50,287 --> 00:39:53,691
through your fingers and
then spring up into the roof.

516
00:39:54,691 --> 00:39:56,793
 NARRATOR: Slowly
 and carefully,

517
00:39:56,893 --> 00:40:00,030
 the divers made it through
 without losing the line,

518
00:40:00,130 --> 00:40:02,533
 this time.

519
00:40:07,137 --> 00:40:10,341
 By late afternoon Jason
 had been caving and diving

520
00:40:10,441 --> 00:40:12,810
 for five hours.

521
00:40:15,112 --> 00:40:19,717
Awaiting them in Chamber 3,
the international rescue team.

522
00:40:21,986 --> 00:40:24,088
JASON: You just knew that
you were seconds away from

523
00:40:24,188 --> 00:40:27,391
surfacing and being able to
pass responsibility for that

524
00:40:27,491 --> 00:40:30,494
boy's life on to
somebody else.

525
00:40:32,329 --> 00:40:35,099
JOSH: The cave line would start
to get some tension on it,

526
00:40:35,199 --> 00:40:37,535
like a fishing line and
so the guys in Chamber 3

527
00:40:37,635 --> 00:40:40,137
would radio up 'fish on'
because that meant a diver

528
00:40:40,237 --> 00:40:42,973
was pulling on the line,
coming toward them.

529
00:40:50,347 --> 00:40:55,152
JASON: I was very
relieved to have got
that first boy out alive.

530
00:40:56,654 --> 00:40:59,523
 NARRATOR: Expert cavers
 and medics took over.

531
00:41:02,358 --> 00:41:05,529
 They carried and hoisted Note
 in a stretcher through the

532
00:41:05,629 --> 00:41:08,899
 final half mile of cave.

533
00:41:20,510 --> 00:41:24,782
 The first four boys were
 out of Tham Luang cave.

534
00:41:24,882 --> 00:41:27,651
 All alive.

535
00:41:27,751 --> 00:41:29,286
 REPORTER (over TV): Mission
 impossible has now become

536
00:41:29,386 --> 00:41:31,255
 mission incredible.

537
00:41:31,355 --> 00:41:32,823
REPORTER (over TV): Well this
is what all of those who've been

538
00:41:32,923 --> 00:41:35,726
 involved in this operation
 have been waiting to see,

539
00:41:35,826 --> 00:41:38,496
 the boys are coming out.

540
00:41:39,496 --> 00:41:41,731
CHRIS: The buzz was amazing.

541
00:41:41,831 --> 00:41:44,701
It was quite incredible that
we got the first four out

542
00:41:44,801 --> 00:41:46,236
we weren't sure we would.

543
00:41:46,336 --> 00:41:48,738
VERN: Emotions were
running high, um,

544
00:41:48,838 --> 00:41:53,177
as you can probably tell,
now, um, absolutely amazing.

545
00:42:01,317 --> 00:42:05,055
NARRATOR: Eight more children
and the coach remained inside.

546
00:42:07,124 --> 00:42:10,927
A further energy-sapping 8
hours of diving and caving for

547
00:42:11,027 --> 00:42:14,164
 each rescuer, lay ahead.

548
00:42:14,831 --> 00:42:17,935
CHRIS: We needed to do it not
once more, but twice more.

549
00:42:23,974 --> 00:42:27,311
 NARRATOR: The divers
 headed back for a
 second group of boys.

550
00:42:27,544 --> 00:42:29,212
 It was another success.

551
00:42:29,746 --> 00:42:32,149
 REPORTER (over TV): Four
 more boys emerging from that

552
00:42:32,249 --> 00:42:34,050
 cramped and flooded cave.

553
00:42:34,150 --> 00:42:36,987
 REPORTER (over TV): All
 are now in hospital in
 nearby Chiang Rai...

554
00:42:43,460 --> 00:42:47,297
 NARRATOR: There were
 just four boys and the
 coach left to rescue.

555
00:42:48,031 --> 00:42:51,000
 But the drama was
 far from over.

556
00:42:51,468 --> 00:42:54,437
 Chris Jewell was diving
 out with the 11th boy,

557
00:42:54,537 --> 00:42:57,541
 13 year old Sompong Jaiwong.

558
00:42:58,708 --> 00:43:00,510
JOSH: It's very easy to
forget the 11th dive is

559
00:43:00,610 --> 00:43:03,180
as dangerous as the 1st dive.

560
00:43:03,280 --> 00:43:07,184
 NARRATOR: Two hours in,
 Chris entered the last sump.

561
00:43:07,284 --> 00:43:09,586
CHRIS: I had the last
bit of diving to do.

562
00:43:09,686 --> 00:43:12,690
I thought I'd sussed it.

563
00:43:14,524 --> 00:43:19,663
 NARRATOR: The 3D data
 reveals the dive line
 goes around a corner,

564
00:43:19,763 --> 00:43:23,033
 where it is pulled
 tight beneath a boulder.

565
00:43:25,402 --> 00:43:29,673
 For Chris, the tension on
 the line proved too much.

566
00:43:32,175 --> 00:43:33,677
CHRIS: Through the process of
going round that corner I was

567
00:43:33,777 --> 00:43:36,846
stretching the line with my
hand and it just slipped out

568
00:43:36,946 --> 00:43:39,550
of my fingers.

569
00:43:43,554 --> 00:43:46,223
When you lose the line
in an underwater cave

570
00:43:46,323 --> 00:43:48,692
that's really bad news.

571
00:43:51,961 --> 00:43:55,432
I couldn't see
which way to go.

572
00:43:58,034 --> 00:44:00,136
 NARRATOR: Time
 was running out,

573
00:44:00,237 --> 00:44:02,539
 both Chris and the
 sedated boy were using up

574
00:44:02,639 --> 00:44:05,776
 their limited air supply.

575
00:44:07,644 --> 00:44:11,348
CHRIS: I was sweeping with my
arms, trying to pick up the line

576
00:44:13,516 --> 00:44:16,654
and I couldn't find the line.

577
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:22,259
The most important
thing is not to panic.

578
00:44:23,493 --> 00:44:26,729
NARRATOR: The data reveals that
as Chris felt for the line

579
00:44:26,830 --> 00:44:30,334
it lay just within arm's reach,

580
00:44:31,234 --> 00:44:33,637
 but in zero visibility,

581
00:44:33,737 --> 00:44:36,540
 finding it was a
 matter of chance.

582
00:44:39,376 --> 00:44:43,446
 After 4 long minutes, Chris
 discovered not the line,

583
00:44:43,546 --> 00:44:46,016
 but an electrical cable,

584
00:44:46,116 --> 00:44:49,118
 laid in the early
 days of the rescue.

585
00:44:50,186 --> 00:44:54,558
 Instead of leading Chris out,
 it led him all the way back,

586
00:44:54,658 --> 00:44:57,827
 to the start of the sump.

587
00:44:58,395 --> 00:45:00,864
CHRIS: Thankfully I realized
I was back somewhere that

588
00:45:00,964 --> 00:45:03,700
I was familiar with.

589
00:45:04,267 --> 00:45:06,903
 NARRATOR: In the dry cave
 Chris found the line and

590
00:45:07,003 --> 00:45:10,007
 continued his rescue.

591
00:45:15,011 --> 00:45:17,147
 Against all the odds,

592
00:45:17,247 --> 00:45:20,417
 the rescuers completed
 their mission.

593
00:45:22,786 --> 00:45:25,689
ITN: They are safe, they
are out, they have done it!

594
00:45:26,023 --> 00:45:29,126
 REPORTER (over TV):
 They have been rescued
 from that flooded cave.

595
00:45:29,226 --> 00:45:32,562
 REPORTER (over TV):
 Millions of people are
 breathing easier tonight.

596
00:45:33,696 --> 00:45:36,667
 NARRATOR: After an intense
 struggle with nature.

597
00:45:37,534 --> 00:45:40,771
 The agonizing wait was over.

598
00:45:43,373 --> 00:45:47,244
VERN: Unreal,
amazing, 13 out of 13,

599
00:45:47,344 --> 00:45:50,547
it's not an unlucky
number anymore.

600
00:45:55,051 --> 00:45:57,821
CHRIS: Things that seem
impossible aren't always so.

601
00:45:57,921 --> 00:46:01,225
Difficult things can be achieved
and amazing things can happen.

602
00:46:01,792 --> 00:46:03,794
PASAKORN: None of us were
doing this out of duty

603
00:46:03,894 --> 00:46:06,930
but out of a desire
to save them.

604
00:46:07,030 --> 00:46:09,566
ROO: I remain in absolute awe
of everybody that took part

605
00:46:09,666 --> 00:46:12,402
and the wonderful
story that this is.

606
00:46:14,871 --> 00:46:18,107
 NARRATOR: Three months
 later, on British TV,

607
00:46:18,207 --> 00:46:21,812
 divers Chris and Jason
 were reunited with the boys

608
00:46:21,912 --> 00:46:25,282
 whose lives they'd saved.

609
00:46:27,284 --> 00:46:29,086
JASON: I didn't know
any of their names.

610
00:46:29,186 --> 00:46:32,890
I remembered them by
numbers 1, 5, 9, and 13.

611
00:46:33,557 --> 00:46:38,829
(applause).

612
00:46:39,896 --> 00:46:42,165
I think they really wanted to
connect with the people that

613
00:46:42,265 --> 00:46:44,033
had brought them out so
it was a really nice,

614
00:46:44,133 --> 00:46:45,869
nice thing that.

615
00:46:45,969 --> 00:46:47,971
TRANSLATOR: You are my heroes,

616
00:46:48,071 --> 00:46:51,908
thank you very much from
the bottom of our hearts.

617
00:46:52,008 --> 00:46:53,710
We love you.

618
00:46:53,810 --> 00:46:56,040
(applause).

